  'A first-semester college music theory course introducing the written, analytical, and practical foundations of tonal musicianship. Students study notation, rhythm and meter, scales, key signatures, intervals, triads, diatonic chords, elementary voice leading, cadences, and melodic analysis while connecting theory to listening, keyboard work, performance, and creative application.',
  $mt1json${"slug": "music-theory-i", "title": "Music Theory I", "description": "A first-semester college music theory course introducing the written, analytical, and practical foundations of tonal musicianship. Students study notation, rhythm and meter, scales, key signatures, intervals, triads, diatonic chords, elementary voice leading, cadences, and melodic analysis while connecting theory to listening, keyboard work, performance, and creative application.", "topics": [{"id": "a3d6a409-f4e4-40ca-b787-ce707892f738", "type": "topic", "title": "Staff, Clefs, and Notation", "description": "This opening unit gives students the notational fluency needed to read, write, analyze, and communicate musical ideas precisely.", "children": [{"id": "a0f1fadc-4cbf-4c6d-ad44-f2673fa929a5", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Pitch notation and the staff", "children": [{"id": "8e12166c-01ad-4658-8f03-5da62e5753b5", "type": "concept", "title": "staff lines and spaces"}, {"id": "a5db0a2e-213e-4dad-8789-47d226912bb3", "type": "concept", "title": "ledger lines"}, {"id": "906235cc-9d9e-427e-a803-538f42e8b785", "type": "concept", "title": "octave designation"}], "description": "Students learn how pitch is represented visually and how notation maps to sound and instruments."}, {"id": "c7bf66bc-f524-4754-93a9-160c3377068c", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Clefs and transposition awareness", "children": [{"id": "b72a4570-f071-43e1-b4ef-4b092a6a9321", "type": "concept", "title": "treble clef"}, {"id": "050b237e-d94a-441b-ac74-78f86c23940e", "type": "concept", "title": "bass clef"}, {"id": "513c53b4-64f9-42f7-9c3d-09945d3b5894", "type": "concept", "title": "C clefs"}], "description": "The class establishes treble, bass, alto, and tenor clef reading foundations."}, {"id": "7b39fdc7-35bc-4a73-af98-f60f36d0302c", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Notational conventions", "children": [{"id": "41dd5b64-4c15-4024-bf07-fc216f57c3af", "type": "concept", "title": "accidentals"}, {"id": "9f6dfd05-fac0-40bb-8421-624ecf9d1fde", "type": "concept", "title": "ties and slurs"}, {"id": "5c8119f5-789d-4713-9ad9-fbd150b0526e", "type": "concept", "title": "articulation and dynamics"}], "description": "Students learn the symbols and layout habits that make scores readable and professional."}]}, {"id": "c65181e1-6998-4ee1-9f73-d9f6d2627b75", "type": "topic", "title": "Rhythm and Meter", "description": "Rhythm and meter organize musical time; students learn to read, count, notate, and hear time structures accurately.", "children": [{"id": "a5866b9a-5a86-49a5-89b9-3c85834b3a2c", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Durations and rests", "children": [{"id": "052c9929-d12b-4e3b-83d0-4fc37313dbf4", "type": "concept", "title": "whole through sixteenth values"}, {"id": "e2c493e1-ab68-4ad8-b0a9-dc6bd80e9565", "type": "concept", "title": "dotted rhythms"}, {"id": "c972e37d-00fd-4549-9f1a-9ea8b4e56dd1", "type": "concept", "title": "ties"}], "description": "Students build confidence with note values, rests, dots, ties, and rhythmic grouping."}, {"id": "b64b0d2d-9330-4073-a879-1a5d1466e75e", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Simple and compound meter", "children": [{"id": "e8d4d106-6698-4724-9b0f-259a997c9580", "type": "concept", "title": "simple meter"}, {"id": "e298d5cd-9e92-47c1-967d-c7d64b9f9be1", "type": "concept", "title": "compound meter"}, {"id": "902e5dba-69ab-429b-a0a4-ffca11e609d0", "type": "concept", "title": "beat subdivision"}], "description": "The unit clarifies how beats divide and how meter shapes musical accent."}, {"id": "c9bf9aaf-cd70-4deb-8c64-a318ea2c9a13", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Syncopation and rhythmic fluency", "children": [{"id": "6d36a41c-2430-4cb5-b67a-192296c2a3af", "type": "concept", "title": "off-beat accents"}, {"id": "29f39e98-e9eb-42b5-a904-79c7b28483eb", "type": "concept", "title": "tuplets"}, {"id": "6a6a27b7-e6d9-48ed-9e9c-6434f8545943", "type": "concept", "title": "counting systems"}], "description": "Students practice rhythmic patterns that occur in classical, jazz, popular, and global repertoires."}]}, {"id": "183d20e1-3953-431a-a075-76cb3bd10b19", "type": "topic", "title": "Major and Minor Scales", "description": "Scales are the vocabulary of tonal music; this unit connects pattern, sound, notation, and function.", "children": [{"id": "9b7d8563-c5de-40b5-8eb4-06a173a667f4", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Major scale structure", "children": [{"id": "c3a5dacd-64d0-4d83-9ccb-519d300329d0", "type": "concept", "title": "whole/half pattern"}, {"id": "f32cf3df-615f-44b2-ac55-f25d8702e7b3", "type": "concept", "title": "scale degrees"}, {"id": "d73c2c20-0710-4ff2-8717-af345c5ce211", "type": "concept", "title": "tonic"}], "description": "Students learn the interval pattern that creates major keys and the sound of tonal stability."}, {"id": "ddab48f8-7c21-45d6-a533-97ff6fb4b07d", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Minor scale forms", "children": [{"id": "a0363be7-1736-46d6-9b46-5d2955570172", "type": "concept", "title": "natural minor"}, {"id": "597723eb-1814-4ead-baf8-6e4905f7b099", "type": "concept", "title": "harmonic minor"}, {"id": "e3fa948e-7998-474a-bb50-444c20317c49", "type": "concept", "title": "melodic minor"}], "description": "The class compares natural, harmonic, and melodic minor as practical tonal tools."}, {"id": "531d95ec-4280-466b-9683-4bb7eaf4f672", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Scale-degree function", "children": [{"id": "c51ee2fe-4436-4f7c-af6c-7a3b7d7c132b", "type": "concept", "title": "tonic"}, {"id": "0cb2f892-bc27-4d38-bfe9-88c3e36061c7", "type": "concept", "title": "dominant"}, {"id": "9d8b8ef1-0357-409f-a654-5b87530304ca", "type": "concept", "title": "leading tone"}], "description": "Students learn names and tendencies that later support melody, harmony, and analysis."}]}, {"id": "3214663e-6660-4ace-81ab-ed0f7feee51c", "type": "topic", "title": "Key Signatures", "description": "Key signatures help students read tonal music efficiently and understand relationships among keys.", "children": [{"id": "fcceb0bd-9d8b-4709-a984-a064052afeb7", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Circle of fifths", "children": [{"id": "b57488ec-b74d-4e1b-b789-833257baba94", "type": "concept", "title": "sharp keys"}, {"id": "e87ce77a-3093-4371-8669-ff5a33fa4d32", "type": "concept", "title": "flat keys"}, {"id": "289440f3-e0d4-41e2-b3f7-2e56eaa3f126", "type": "concept", "title": "enharmonic keys"}], "description": "Students learn the pattern connecting keys, accidentals, and closely related tonal areas."}, {"id": "68aa3bf5-19ec-4676-a8a5-a6c45a250902", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Major and relative minor keys", "children": [{"id": "1fd8b78c-34e7-442c-9d48-c6fa35c827b7", "type": "concept", "title": "relative minor"}, {"id": "3f465f81-f8bd-40bf-a89a-a188ab1fdcb4", "type": "concept", "title": "parallel minor"}, {"id": "0506266d-e87b-4ffc-9ace-c91728d4992b", "type": "concept", "title": "tonic identification"}], "description": "The unit links each key signature to major and minor tonal possibilities."}, {"id": "36e1639d-b182-4033-a9f9-f4ed2b4b254b", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Applied key fluency", "children": [{"id": "91843bd0-449c-49af-920e-b73319b38037", "type": "concept", "title": "key signature drills"}, {"id": "8a7d88cd-fc1a-49f2-ac7e-9845017e35a2", "type": "concept", "title": "scale writing"}, {"id": "4173f591-93ca-498c-a335-eab8dea7dd11", "type": "concept", "title": "aural/key recognition"}], "description": "Students practice identifying, writing, and using keys in short musical examples."}]}, {"id": "ee9ddb5f-340e-4e3d-936c-19ec02c8ad56", "type": "topic", "title": "Intervals", "description": "Intervals are the building blocks of melody and harmony; this unit develops precise identification, spelling, and listening.", "children": [{"id": "a53e310e-8762-412f-a70e-27305efaef2f", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Interval size and quality", "children": [{"id": "42c90a9e-da64-4349-9b24-3ddbd10d33f1", "type": "concept", "title": "perfect intervals"}, {"id": "d07d1333-2f26-43c3-8203-a6ab3c7e8aaa", "type": "concept", "title": "major/minor intervals"}, {"id": "66e9ba3c-8507-4a48-af77-9502b6f7af17", "type": "concept", "title": "augmented/diminished intervals"}], "description": "Students learn to label intervals accurately by number and quality."}, {"id": "b5ba7c5a-03fd-4a3a-809f-44131868dc4b", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Melodic and harmonic intervals", "children": [{"id": "55be39fd-b4df-49bd-9e38-41eb2323b71a", "type": "concept", "title": "ascending intervals"}, {"id": "0dfdf47f-51e0-4466-8c73-35afa4606258", "type": "concept", "title": "descending intervals"}, {"id": "1c509669-2c83-4aa2-8374-0aee88498745", "type": "concept", "title": "harmonic intervals"}], "description": "The class connects interval notation to both sequential and simultaneous sound."}, {"id": "32be0c9e-2c3c-4c26-af32-9e2e351f5fec", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Consonance, dissonance, and tendency", "children": [{"id": "187806f6-f917-4b7c-9db4-a21c3c149c73", "type": "concept", "title": "perfect consonance"}, {"id": "5aab01d3-b08e-4984-8ffe-ec40dcd6c4a2", "type": "concept", "title": "imperfect consonance"}, {"id": "8a25c73e-fb97-4da6-9323-0dc4de523e13", "type": "concept", "title": "dissonance"}], "description": "Students begin to hear why intervals feel stable, tense, or directional."}]}, {"id": "d609f33e-a975-4660-a422-30a962b045b5", "type": "topic", "title": "Triads and Chord Qualities", "description": "Triads introduce vertical harmony and prepare students for harmonic analysis, part-writing, and keyboard application.", "children": [{"id": "11039158-f33e-450c-b5cd-2566adeda3f3", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Building triads", "children": [{"id": "99fffe55-d28d-442f-8987-1add20c1dd0d", "type": "concept", "title": "root"}, {"id": "970e474b-43c9-440e-81e9-3473003e21f3", "type": "concept", "title": "third"}, {"id": "10f3161c-f01e-4b6c-a154-23e9155a6e2b", "type": "concept", "title": "fifth"}], "description": "Students learn to construct triads by stacking thirds from any root."}, {"id": "9babf9e8-b799-40de-805f-980a986bf2b7", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Triad qualities", "children": [{"id": "1c206bf2-681f-4cbf-82a8-0fa89a0c9ce0", "type": "concept", "title": "major triads"}, {"id": "f30108a9-dc14-444b-a548-3367d5a79bbd", "type": "concept", "title": "minor triads"}, {"id": "f6e84935-0d95-4843-9bc1-af1a6bdd3b0d", "type": "concept", "title": "diminished/augmented triads"}], "description": "The class distinguishes major, minor, diminished, and augmented sonorities by spelling and sound."}, {"id": "3b2e449b-695f-4100-b968-d324ccbf6c01", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Inversions and figured bass basics", "children": [{"id": "7af145a5-6277-4cfc-8fb4-2d0b29663ce5", "type": "concept", "title": "root position"}, {"id": "6a61f86c-ccae-4c6c-a1b0-e9b035749f34", "type": "concept", "title": "first inversion"}, {"id": "1a07a159-0850-4eb1-911f-a29a6319c47e", "type": "concept", "title": "second inversion"}], "description": "Students learn how bass position changes chord notation and voice-leading possibilities."}]}, {"id": "a0fc3de5-cb88-4e5e-a12f-6165f5febbed", "type": "topic", "title": "Diatonic Chords", "description": "This unit connects scales to harmony, showing how chords belong to keys and how Roman numerals describe function.", "children": [{"id": "ddcb23f0-c111-4d76-a4a0-6aee74ed983d", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Harmonizing the scale", "children": [{"id": "45a98094-2c4d-415e-927f-1a39e954f580", "type": "concept", "title": "diatonic triads"}, {"id": "485d9abd-7f0a-495b-b780-cf1761e85554", "type": "concept", "title": "scale-degree roots"}, {"id": "b55286ae-0d8c-4f17-9b87-24f9c4018328", "type": "concept", "title": "quality patterns"}], "description": "Students build triads on each scale degree in major and minor keys."}, {"id": "4e901915-306e-479a-bb99-8b706dfde65a", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Roman numeral analysis", "children": [{"id": "1c93742a-b9a8-45f2-94ff-f4203ed9045c", "type": "concept", "title": "uppercase/lowercase numerals"}, {"id": "35a98dea-1990-4abf-80ae-71477628dd1b", "type": "concept", "title": "inversion figures"}, {"id": "13966459-1d8c-49a5-abad-c710aeb15f2d", "type": "concept", "title": "key context"}], "description": "The class introduces a durable symbolic system for comparing harmony across keys."}, {"id": "b254cc33-4146-498a-bbdd-1a0202145d56", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Basic harmonic function", "children": [{"id": "abf3d60c-02f3-433f-897a-71dd9c41a48c", "type": "concept", "title": "tonic area"}, {"id": "90a9deb9-5c99-4ebd-a420-fba18c80cfa2", "type": "concept", "title": "predominant area"}, {"id": "2c95ac25-3e1b-42ff-9fa4-0e0af8cb81dc", "type": "concept", "title": "dominant area"}], "description": "Students learn the first layer of tonic, predominant, and dominant behavior."}]}, {"id": "58604926-b673-4a8c-9d4e-386f1e549884", "type": "topic", "title": "Basic Part-Writing", "description": "Part-writing turns chord knowledge into musical voice leading, training students to write clear, singable lines.", "children": [{"id": "3bb13406-8632-4082-9f22-f8394f89a79f", "type": "subtopic", "title": "SATB texture", "children": [{"id": "6772fdcc-aee7-4264-9e39-39a50ce02fb5", "type": "concept", "title": "voice ranges"}, {"id": "e297cb51-6623-4965-a61c-22168653845d", "type": "concept", "title": "open/close spacing"}, {"id": "c95e2017-3f4d-4da2-985a-685a16668921", "type": "concept", "title": "doubling"}], "description": "Students learn the ranges, spacing, and roles of soprano, alto, tenor, and bass."}, {"id": "932c1aa0-3e81-41aa-b320-cf1e0c4b38f6", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Voice-leading principles", "children": [{"id": "60d489b2-4db5-44f5-aeb8-2a769a5a7aab", "type": "concept", "title": "stepwise motion"}, {"id": "0db1ce0b-61c0-4dbd-9973-8f3740bbf2cf", "type": "concept", "title": "common tones"}, {"id": "d117a5ec-b4f3-4b0d-b030-5fee64542b5e", "type": "concept", "title": "parallel fifths/octaves"}], "description": "The unit establishes smooth motion and common-practice constraints."}, {"id": "11a968c4-e4cc-4764-bdd6-9b8fc58867a4", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Writing simple progressions", "children": [{"id": "c1efce2e-155d-4b34-a3e3-a1c5f3627493", "type": "concept", "title": "I-V-I"}, {"id": "21090c43-8d9b-4ebb-a122-573fc0973595", "type": "concept", "title": "I-IV-V-I"}, {"id": "a6bdf9be-663f-40aa-8ad6-8ea0227f99c1", "type": "concept", "title": "root-position writing"}], "description": "Students apply chord knowledge in short harmonizations and cadential patterns."}]}, {"id": "f154ea2d-163e-4d32-862e-7597d66ae17f", "type": "topic", "title": "Cadences", "description": "Cadences shape musical punctuation; students learn how harmony, melody, and phrase design create closure or continuation.", "children": [{"id": "ccc8092e-efdd-4070-a508-500ede57fc77", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Cadence types", "children": [{"id": "66e69a6b-f698-4552-85ca-33b365f04169", "type": "concept", "title": "authentic cadence"}, {"id": "e0848ef1-6cf8-4f8b-a4a8-76709c835010", "type": "concept", "title": "half cadence"}, {"id": "cfb7f1f1-53cc-4d86-a0a2-6ef14e76fe61", "type": "concept", "title": "plagal/deceptive cadence"}], "description": "Students identify and write common cadence formulas."}, {"id": "d428b939-89c2-45a0-bc13-d5bb020de017", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Phrase endings", "children": [{"id": "208f4f65-9ac6-47a5-b124-db9d485611c2", "type": "concept", "title": "phrase rhythm"}, {"id": "c04ff21e-c0fc-4540-8f29-171582ae9192", "type": "concept", "title": "arrival tones"}, {"id": "8d9b6495-8538-4c00-b443-a71a31dab36c", "type": "concept", "title": "cadential bass motion"}], "description": "The class connects cadences to melodic goal points and formal structure."}, {"id": "47f9a10a-1cb1-4bb5-8099-ce9d31a68697", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Cadences in repertoire", "children": [{"id": "769c1b3d-b308-434e-a2e3-247b6efdf62a", "type": "concept", "title": "score excerpts"}, {"id": "a123b4a4-9afe-42d1-a5cf-a48106ffaf60", "type": "concept", "title": "listening examples"}, {"id": "b277320b-3300-4153-96ed-71fa4d90c9fd", "type": "concept", "title": "cadence labeling"}], "description": "Students analyze short excerpts to hear how cadence affects expectation."}]}, {"id": "bcc8d81e-14f0-406a-b681-7253e64c3b9c", "type": "topic", "title": "Melodic Analysis", "description": "Melodic analysis helps students understand how lines are shaped by contour, motive, rhythm, phrase, and harmony.", "children": [{"id": "89c4f299-109d-437b-9d92-28a95f661f6b", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Contour and range", "children": [{"id": "b0004073-d5e2-4c6e-a4ed-2901e2e145c6", "type": "concept", "title": "high point"}, {"id": "b6df597d-f7c3-452a-8776-1e7f58539645", "type": "concept", "title": "low point"}, {"id": "c3aa58e9-2985-4f8d-9ea1-7a17df7d3871", "type": "concept", "title": "tessitura"}], "description": "Students describe the shape and span of melodies using clear analytical language."}, {"id": "def87193-5e04-4d0e-aeb5-aafe1118f2bc", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Motive and sequence", "children": [{"id": "e03e6a92-2c47-4477-a8f1-06cbb02ddcd1", "type": "concept", "title": "motivic cells"}, {"id": "0f98464a-eb72-45b9-9285-9164eec48436", "type": "concept", "title": "sequence"}, {"id": "9e2373dd-27fc-4573-bec8-34472b927f1b", "type": "concept", "title": "fragmentation"}], "description": "The unit introduces repetition, variation, and development at the phrase level."}, {"id": "a354c3eb-ec9c-49a4-8aeb-9ed6a7b5aa51", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Phrase and harmonic implication", "children": [{"id": "89b6b124-731c-450c-8c2a-a08a11944374", "type": "concept", "title": "phrase structure"}, {"id": "7ade2af1-bbb1-4d92-88fd-0bb12fdf6afa", "type": "concept", "title": "cadential tones"}, {"id": "f79a5561-34d1-4280-8b0f-577e8c8a6099", "type": "concept", "title": "non-chord tones preview"}], "description": "Students connect melody to cadences, scale degrees, and implied harmony."}]}, {"id": "bfeaf91d-385a-4b0c-bc45-8f750ec25dcb", "type": "topic", "title": "Listening, Keyboard, and Musicianship Integration", "description": "This added world-class unit prevents theory from becoming paper-only by connecting concepts to sound, singing, and keyboard practice.", "children": [{"id": "d98b9b6a-635b-43d3-81ce-7088535fc3f1", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Aural reinforcement", "children": [{"id": "7fb2ae5f-e5a5-424b-9c21-1ebfae11d535", "type": "concept", "title": "interval singing"}, {"id": "d377e8b0-4bce-49ee-bd00-c384d75cdd6a", "type": "concept", "title": "scale-degree hearing"}, {"id": "64a8d7f3-9db4-47eb-9603-c8c5bb3c11ae", "type": "concept", "title": "cadence recognition"}], "description": "Students hear and sing the concepts they write on the page."}, {"id": "1d8b18d2-8a88-42b0-95f9-dc6dc8b1f041", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Keyboard application", "children": [{"id": "c4a23511-e61d-49d6-9ccf-7ac2870b912b", "type": "concept", "title": "scale playing"}, {"id": "9f0fdd2f-69be-46fa-906c-d66bdd99d290", "type": "concept", "title": "triad drills"}, {"id": "f4c92eaa-8626-46d8-9dd3-f931aa05af16", "type": "concept", "title": "cadence patterns"}], "description": "The class uses simple keyboard tasks to embody scales, chords, and progressions."}, {"id": "f9990de3-fbab-443a-b523-de2a37cf38cc", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Analysis-to-performance transfer", "children": [{"id": "6fdc9360-d199-4efc-a9b5-e6070dd692e2", "type": "concept", "title": "phrase shaping"}, {"id": "dc14d44b-e71f-4a09-b96c-45a6e28ee9ef", "type": "concept", "title": "harmonic arrival"}, {"id": "2a641ef9-646a-4621-b760-180baed61793", "type": "concept", "title": "melodic tendency tones"}], "description": "Students learn how theory informs phrasing, emphasis, tuning, and interpretation."}]}, {"id": "0bfe8730-a716-462c-bb5d-20a5d083c679", "type": "topic", "title": "Contemporary and Cross-Genre Applications", "description": "This added capstone unit makes the course more current by applying core theory to classical, popular, jazz-adjacent, and media examples.", "children": [{"id": "d2be177b-13c0-40d4-ad7c-d25cb39d3004", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Lead-sheet and chord-symbol bridge", "children": [{"id": "94ea7e47-fdaf-488c-8d48-3d791d1544a9", "type": "concept", "title": "major/minor symbols"}, {"id": "0f5e5333-506b-40b9-a3bb-fc52fba5cf41", "type": "concept", "title": "slash chords preview"}, {"id": "648e580a-0884-4a67-a715-9d11a65fb880", "type": "concept", "title": "basic seventh-chord preview"}], "description": "Students connect Roman numerals and triads to common chord-symbol practice."}, {"id": "fc8f9286-4526-49c4-bc76-472beabfe8ff", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Popular and film examples", "children": [{"id": "9dea43e6-cdd7-4490-a1c4-a1c90f96a1f8", "type": "concept", "title": "loop progressions"}, {"id": "d7309201-c43b-4dbf-9b7d-f405a3a40b1b", "type": "concept", "title": "modal mixture preview"}, {"id": "18c7e758-2346-4ca4-9dd1-d7de95c8e9f6", "type": "concept", "title": "riff-based melody"}], "description": "The class analyzes short examples beyond the common-practice canon."}, {"id": "6701aecd-8952-4c64-9275-e53c07694bd7", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Creative theory task", "children": [{"id": "faa32fbf-e22e-41bb-a8cb-12bc177dc659", "type": "concept", "title": "melody writing"}, {"id": "054fa3d3-b6ef-41e7-a9bb-ab6b06cf22b0", "type": "concept", "title": "harmonization"}, {"id": "3faf7ea9-b514-4e02-9e50-cea3561fcea9", "type": "concept", "title": "cadential design"}], "description": "Students compose or arrange a short example using course concepts."}]}], "dbBacked": true}$mt1json$::jsonb,
